      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Make a video explaining how password reset works in our web app: the user says they forgot their password, the app looks up their account, emails them a one-time link, and the user opens it and chooses a new password."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The graph is saved. It shows the user, the web app and its users database inside your team's backend zone, and the external email service. The flow runs from the forgotten password request, through the account lookup and the emailed one-time link, to the new password and sign-in.\n\nI assumed the email service is an external provider and that the reset link opens in the same web app. Does the graph look right, or would you like changes?",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The graph looks good. I approve it."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The graph is approved. Before I write the script, let's agree the story. Here's what I propose:\n\n- **Audience:** People who use the app, not its developers.\n- **Shape:** Problem, how it works, outcome.\n- **Hook:** \"Someone can't remember their password.\"\n- **Takeaway:** \"A reset link works once, and only for an hour.\"\n\nThe script would run in about five scenes-worth of beats: the user asks for help, the app finds the account, the one-time link goes out by email, the user opens it and picks a new password, and they end up signed in.\n\nShould I go ahead with this story, or change the audience, takeaway or hook?",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Yes, that story works for me. Go ahead and write the script."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've written the script: one scene with seven beats, about 40 seconds long (estimated until the narration is generated). It opens on the user forgetting their password and ends with them signed in, with the one-time link, which works once and only for an hour, as the callout.\n\nDoes the script look right, or would you like changes?",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The script looks good. I approve it."
      },
